## Summary

Extracted **12 program graphs** from the Compound V2 cTokens specification at `https://docs.compound.finance/v2/ctokens/`. All `.mmd` files were written to `/Users/hiro/Documents/security-agent/outputs/graphs/batch_w2b2_1773060675/compound-v2-ctokens/`.

### Subgraphs Extracted

| ID | Function | Description | Key Invariants |
|:---|:---------|:------------|:---------------|
| SG-001 | `mint` | Supply underlying assets, receive cTokens | Exchange rate conservation, totalSupply increase matches mintAmount/exchangeRate |
| SG-002 | `redeem` | Convert cTokens back to underlying (by cToken amount) | redeemAmount = redeemTokens * exchangeRate, liquidity check |
| SG-003 | `redeemUnderlying` | Convert cTokens back to underlying (by underlying amount) | redeemTokens = redeemAmount / exchangeRate, liquidity check |
| SG-004 | `borrow` | Borrow underlying assets against collateral | Cash sufficiency, collateral adequacy, totalBorrows tracking |
| SG-005 | `repayBorrow` | Repay own borrow balance | uint(-1) full repay logic, balance/total decrement consistency |
| SG-006 | `repayBorrowBehalf` | Repay another user's borrow | Funds from msg.sender, borrower's debt reduced |
| SG-007 | `transfer` | ERC-20 transfer with liquidity guard | Token conservation, liquidity check for entered markets |
| SG-008 | `liquidateBorrow` | Liquidate underwater account | Self-liquidation prevention, close factor limit, seize calculation with liquidation incentive |
| SG-009 | `exchangeRateCurrent` | Calculate cToken-to-underlying exchange rate | Monotonically non-decreasing, formula: (cash + borrows - reserves) / supply |
| SG-010 | `accrueInterest` | Accumulate interest across blocks | Simple interest model, reserve factor split, borrowIndex update, idempotent within block |
| SG-011 | `borrowBalanceCurrent` | Get current borrow balance with interest | principal * borrowIndex / accountInterestIndex |
| SG-012 | `balanceOfUnderlying` | Get underlying balance for cToken holder | cTokenBalance * exchangeRate |

Each program graph follows the formal PG = (Q, q_init, q_final, Act, E) structure with `note right of` blocks encoding invariants. All graphs include error paths matching the specification's error codes and failure info.

